{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":13948409}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# AI-real generation pipeline (refactored)\n\nGenerates the **fact-preserving** (AI-real) class for BanglaShieldBERT.\n\n**Generation settings are intentionally unchanged** from parts 81-100 so the dataset stays\nconsistent. What is new: validation, metadata logging, crash-safe saving, and API key\nrotation.\n\nRun cells in order. Cell 1 is the only one you normally edit.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# CELL 1 — CONFIGURATION  (this is the only cell you edit)\n# ============================================================\n\nFILE_NUM = 81                      # which news_part_N.xlsx to process\nDATASET_SLUG = \"news_splti_news_81_100\"\n\n# --- API keys -------------------------------------------------\nINLINE_KEYS = []          # leave empty; only a fallback\n\ndef load_keys(max_keys=8):\n    try:\n        from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n        secrets = UserSecretsClient()\n    except Exception:\n        return [k for k in INLINE_KEYS if k.strip()]\n\n    keys = []\n    for n in range(1, max_keys + 1):\n        try:\n            k = secrets.get_secret(f\"GROQ_KEY_{n}\").strip()\n            if k:\n                keys.append(k)\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n    return keys or [k for k in INLINE_KEYS if k.strip()]\n\nGROQ_API_KEYS = load_keys()\nfor i, k in enumerate(GROQ_API_KEYS, 1):\n    print(f\"key {i}: {k[:6]}...{k[-4:]}\")\n# --- generation settings: DO NOT CHANGE MID-DATASET -----------\n# These must match whatever parts 1-60 used, otherwise you introduce\n# a distribution shift between parts of your own dataset.\nMODEL_NAME            = \"openai/gpt-oss-120b\"\nMODEL_MAX_TOKENS      = 2500     # self-imposed prompt+output budget\nDEFAULT_OUTPUT_TOKENS = 1000     # reserved for the model's reply\nSAFETY_MARGIN_TOKENS  = 32\nMAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS = 1024\nTEMPERATURE           = 1.0\nTOP_P                 = 0.8\nREASONING_EFFORT      = None     # None = same as parts 1-60.\n                                 # \"low\" frees up output budget but CHANGES the\n                                 # output distribution — only switch if you plan\n                                 # to regenerate parts 1-60 too.\n\n# --- pacing ---------------------------------------------------\n# Free tier gpt-oss-120b is roughly 8K tokens/min, so ~1 request per\n# 17s. Lower this only on the dev tier.\nBASE_DELAY_SEC = 15\nMAX_DELAY_SEC  = 180\nMAX_RETRIES    = 8\n\n# --- quality gates --------------------------------------------\nMIN_BANGLA_RATIO = 0.85   # share of letters that must be Bengali script\nMIN_BODY_WORDS   = 30     # shorter than this is treated as a failed generation\nMAX_TITLE_WORDS  = 30     # longer than this means line 1 was not a headline\n\n# --- io -------------------------------------------------------\nWORKING_DIR   = \"/kaggle/working\"\nSAVE_EVERY    = 20        # rows between full Excel writes (JSONL is per-row)\nRETRY_FAILURES = True     # re-attempt rows that previously failed validation\n\nprint(f\"Config loaded — part {FILE_NUM}, {len([k for k in GROQ_API_KEYS if k])} key(s)\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-16T21:00:24.667177Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-16T21:00:24.667528Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-16T21:00:25.022852Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-16T21:00:24.667488Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-16T21:00:25.022004Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# CELL 2 — IMPORTS, PATHS, VALIDATION HELPERS\n# ============================================================\n!pip install -q groq pandas openpyxl tqdm tiktoken\n\nimport os, re, json, time, unicodedata\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nimport pandas as pd\nimport tiktoken\nfrom tqdm.auto import tqdm\n\nenc = tiktoken.get_encoding(\"cl100k_base\")   # approximation only — see note below\n\ndef count_tokens(text: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Approximate token count.\n\n    cl100k_base is NOT gpt-oss's tokenizer and over-counts Bangla, so this\n    over-estimates. Kept deliberately: parts 1-60 were budgeted with the same\n    function, and consistency matters more than accuracy here.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return 0\n    return len(enc.encode(text))\n\n\n# ---------- file discovery ----------\ndef find_input_file(part_num: int) -> str:\n    target = f\"news_part_{part_num}.xlsx\"\n    for path in (f\"/kaggle/input/{DATASET_SLUG}/{target}\",\n                 f\"/kaggle/input/{target}\"):\n        if os.path.exists(path):\n            return path\n    if os.path.exists(\"/kaggle/input\"):\n        for root, _, files in os.walk(\"/kaggle/input\"):\n            if target in files:\n                return os.path.join(root, target)\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\n        f\"Could not find '{target}' under /kaggle/input/. \"\n        f\"Add the dataset via + Add Input in the sidebar.\"\n    )\n\n\nINPUT_PATH  = find_input_file(FILE_NUM)\nOUTPUT_PATH = os.path.join(WORKING_DIR, f\"ai_real_part_{FILE_NUM}.xlsx\")\nJSONL_PATH  = os.path.join(WORKING_DIR, f\"ai_real_part_{FILE_NUM}.jsonl\")\n\n\n# ---------- output validation ----------\nBENGALI_RANGE = (0x0980, 0x09FF)\n\ndef bangla_ratio(text: str) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Share of alphabetic characters that fall in the Bengali Unicode block.\n\n    Digits, punctuation and whitespace are ignored, so '২০২৪ সালে' scores 1.0\n    while 'ঢাকায় protest হয়েছে' scores well below it.\n    \"\"\"\n    letters = [ch for ch in text if ch.isalpha()]\n    if not letters:\n        return 0.0\n    bengali = sum(1 for ch in letters\n                  if BENGALI_RANGE[0] <= ord(ch) <= BENGALI_RANGE[1])\n    return bengali / len(letters)\n\n\nLABEL_PREFIXES = (\"শিরোনাম:\", \"সংবাদ:\", \"প্রতিবেদন:\", \"Headline:\", \"Body:\", \"Title:\", \"News:\")\n\ndef clean_line(line: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Strip markdown and label prefixes.\n\n    Order matters: '**শিরোনাম:** রাজশাহীতে...' leaves a stray '**' behind if you\n    remove the prefix before the emphasis markers, so emphasis goes first and the\n    prefix pass loops (a label can sit behind a bullet behind a bold marker).\n    \"\"\"\n    line = line.strip()\n    line = re.sub(r\"[*_`]+\", \"\", line)              # markdown emphasis anywhere\n    line = re.sub(r\"^[#>\\-\\u2022\\s]+\", \"\", line)    # headers, bullets, dashes\n    for _ in range(3):\n        stripped = False\n        for p in LABEL_PREFIXES:\n            if line.startswith(p):\n                line = line[len(p):].strip()\n                stripped = True\n        if not stripped:\n            break\n    return line.strip()\n\n\ndef parse_output(raw: str):\n    \"\"\"Split the model reply into (headline, body). Returns ('', '') if unusable.\"\"\"\n    lines = [clean_line(l) for l in raw.splitlines()]\n    lines = [l for l in lines if l and l not in LABEL_PREFIXES]\n    if not lines:\n        return \"\", \"\"\n    title = lines[0]\n    body  = \"\\n\".join(lines[1:]).strip()\n    return title, body\n\n\ndef validate(title: str, body: str, finish_reason: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return 'ok' or a short failure code. Failure codes are retried later.\"\"\"\n    if not title or not body:\n        return \"empty\"\n    if finish_reason == \"length\":\n        return \"cut_off\"\n    if len(body.split()) < MIN_BODY_WORDS:\n        return \"too_short\"\n    if len(title.split()) > MAX_TITLE_WORDS:\n        return \"bad_title\"\n    if bangla_ratio(title + \" \" + body) < MIN_BANGLA_RATIO:\n        return \"low_bangla\"\n    return \"ok\"\n\n\n# ---------- crash-safe saving ----------\ndef atomic_to_excel(df: pd.DataFrame, path: str):\n    \"\"\"Write to a temp file, then rename. A crash mid-write leaves the old file intact.\"\"\"\n    base, ext = os.path.splitext(path)     # keep .xlsx so pandas picks the right engine\n    tmp = f\"{base}.tmp{ext}\"\n    df.to_excel(tmp, index=False)\n    os.replace(tmp, path)\n\n\ndef append_jsonl(record: dict, path: str = JSONL_PATH):\n    with open(path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n\nprint(f\"Input : {INPUT_PATH}\")\nprint(f\"Output: {OUTPUT_PATH}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-16T21:29:39.099361Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-16T21:29:39.099696Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-16T21:29:43.250354Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-16T21:29:39.09967Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-16T21:29:43.249323Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# CELL 3 — CLIENT, KEY ROTATION, GENERATION\n# ============================================================\nfrom groq import Groq\n\nSYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = \"\"\"\nYou are a professional Bangla newspaper reporter.\nRewrite the provided news update into a clean, natural newspaper report in standard Bangla.\nRules:\n1. Write strictly in pure Bangla script. Do NOT output Chinese, English, or foreign characters.\n2. Maintain strict factual fidelity to the original text. Do NOT add unverified facts.\n3. Do NOT include prefix labels like 'শিরোনাম:' or 'সংবাদ:'.\n4. Line 1 MUST be the news headline ONLY.\n5. Line 2 onwards MUST be the news body report ONLY.\n\"\"\"\n\n_keys = [k.strip() for k in GROQ_API_KEYS if k and k.strip()]\nif not _keys:\n    raise ValueError(\"No API keys set in GROQ_API_KEYS (Cell 1).\")\n\n_key_idx = 0\nclient = Groq(api_key=_keys[_key_idx])\ncurrent_delay = BASE_DELAY_SEC\n\n\ndef rotate_key() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Move to the next key. Returns False when every key is exhausted.\"\"\"\n    global _key_idx, client, current_delay\n    if _key_idx + 1 >= len(_keys):\n        return False\n    _key_idx += 1\n    client = Groq(api_key=_keys[_key_idx])\n    current_delay = BASE_DELAY_SEC\n    print(f\"Switched to API key #{_key_idx + 1} of {len(_keys)}\")\n    return True\n\n\ndef truncate_to_budget(content: str, title: str):\n    \"\"\"Trim content on word boundaries so the whole request fits MODEL_MAX_TOKENS.\n\n    Returns (content_to_send, was_truncated).\n    \"\"\"\n    estimated = (count_tokens(SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION) + count_tokens(title)\n                 + count_tokens(content) + DEFAULT_OUTPUT_TOKENS + SAFETY_MARGIN_TOKENS)\n    if estimated <= MODEL_MAX_TOKENS:\n        return content, False\n\n    budget = count_tokens(content) - (estimated - MODEL_MAX_TOKENS) - 10\n    if budget <= 0:\n        return \"\", True\n\n    words, lo, hi, best = content.split(), 0, len(content.split()), \"\"\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        candidate = \" \".join(words[:mid])\n        if count_tokens(candidate) <= budget:\n            best, lo = candidate, mid + 1\n        else:\n            hi = mid - 1\n    return best, True\n\n\ndef generate(title: str, content: str):\n    \"\"\"One API call with retry + key rotation.\n\n    Returns (raw_text, finish_reason). Raises only on unrecoverable failure.\n    \"\"\"\n    global current_delay\n\n    kwargs = dict(\n        model=MODEL_NAME,\n        messages=[\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION},\n            {\"role\": \"user\",   \"content\": f\"শিরোনাম:\\n{title}\\n\\nসংবাদ:\\n{content}\"},\n        ],\n        max_completion_tokens=MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS,\n        temperature=TEMPERATURE,\n        top_p=TOP_P,\n    )\n    if REASONING_EFFORT:\n        kwargs[\"reasoning_effort\"] = REASONING_EFFORT\n\n    for attempt in range(MAX_RETRIES):\n        try:\n            resp = client.chat.completions.create(**kwargs)\n            text = resp.choices[0].message.content or \"\"\n            reason = resp.choices[0].finish_reason or \"unknown\"\n\n            if current_delay > BASE_DELAY_SEC:\n                current_delay = max(BASE_DELAY_SEC, current_delay - 5)\n            return text.strip(), reason\n\n        except Exception as e:\n            msg = str(e).lower()\n            is_rate = \"429\" in msg or \"rate\" in msg or \"limit\" in msg or \"quota\" in msg\n            daily_gone = \"day\" in msg or \"rpd\" in msg or \"tpd\" in msg\n\n            if not is_rate:\n                raise\n\n            if daily_gone and rotate_key():\n                continue\n\n            current_delay = min(MAX_DELAY_SEC,\n                                30 if current_delay < 30 else current_delay + 30)\n            print(f\"  rate limited — waiting {current_delay}s \"\n                  f\"(attempt {attempt + 1}/{MAX_RETRIES})\")\n            time.sleep(current_delay)\n\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Exhausted retries and API keys.\")\n\n\nprint(f\"Ready — {MODEL_NAME}, {len(_keys)} key(s), base delay {BASE_DELAY_SEC}s\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-16T21:29:50.416833Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-16T21:29:50.417206Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-16T21:29:50.501656Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-16T21:29:50.417168Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-16T21:29:50.500633Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# one-time recovery: rebuild the checkpoint from the JSONL log\nimport json\n\ndf = pd.read_excel(INPUT_PATH)[[\"news_title\", \"news_content\"]].copy()\nfor col, default in {\n    \"ai_generated_news_title\": \"\", \"ai_generated_news_content\": \"\",\n    \"gen_status\": \"\", \"finish_reason\": \"\", \"source_truncated\": False,\n    \"bangla_ratio\": 0.0, \"body_words\": 0, \"gen_model\": \"\", \"gen_time_utc\": \"\",\n}.items():\n    df[col] = default\n\nn = 0\nwith open(JSONL_PATH, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    for line in f:\n        r = json.loads(line)\n        i = r[\"row\"]\n        if r.get(\"status\") == \"error\" or i >= len(df):\n            continue\n        df.at[i, \"ai_generated_news_title\"]   = r.get(\"title\", \"\")\n        df.at[i, \"ai_generated_news_content\"] = r.get(\"content\", \"\")\n        df.at[i, \"gen_status\"]       = r.get(\"status\", \"\")\n        df.at[i, \"finish_reason\"]    = r.get(\"finish_reason\", \"\")\n        df.at[i, \"source_truncated\"] = r.get(\"source_truncated\", False)\n        df.at[i, \"bangla_ratio\"]     = r.get(\"bangla_ratio\", 0.0)\n        df.at[i, \"body_words\"]       = r.get(\"body_words\", 0)\n        n += 1\n\natomic_to_excel(df, OUTPUT_PATH)\nprint(f\"recovered {n} rows -> {OUTPUT_PATH}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-16T21:29:56.486233Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-16T21:29:56.486612Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-16T21:29:57.713079Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-16T21:29:56.486582Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-16T21:29:57.712073Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# CELL 4 — MAIN LOOP\n# ============================================================\n\nMETA_COLS = {\n    \"ai_generated_news_title\":   \"\",\n    \"ai_generated_news_content\": \"\",\n    \"gen_status\":                \"\",     # ok / empty / cut_off / low_bangla / error:...\n    \"finish_reason\":             \"\",\n    \"source_truncated\":          False,\n    \"bangla_ratio\":              0.0,\n    \"body_words\":                0,\n    \"gen_model\":                 \"\",\n    \"gen_time_utc\":              \"\",\n}\n\n# resume from checkpoint if one exists\nif os.path.exists(OUTPUT_PATH):\n    df = pd.read_excel(OUTPUT_PATH)\n    print(f\"Resuming from checkpoint — {len(df)} rows\")\nelse:\n    df = pd.read_excel(INPUT_PATH)[[\"news_title\", \"news_content\"]].copy()\n    print(f\"Fresh start — {len(df)} rows\")\n\nfor col, default in META_COLS.items():\n    if col not in df.columns:\n        df[col] = default\n\nRETRYABLE = {\"\", \"empty\", \"cut_off\", \"low_bangla\", \"too_short\", \"bad_title\"}\n\ndef needs_work(row) -> bool:\n    status = str(row.get(\"gen_status\", \"\") or \"\").strip()\n    if status == \"ok\":\n        return False\n    if status.startswith(\"error\") or status in RETRYABLE:\n        return RETRY_FAILURES or status == \"\"\n    return True\n\ntodo = [i for i, r in df.iterrows() if needs_work(r)]\nprint(f\"{len(todo)} rows to process, {len(df) - len(todo)} already done\\n\")\n\nprocessed = 0\nfor i in tqdm(todo, desc=f\"Part {FILE_NUM}\"):\n    title   = str(df.at[i, \"news_title\"]).strip()\n    content = str(df.at[i, \"news_content\"]).strip()\n\n    try:\n        content_to_send, was_truncated = truncate_to_budget(content, title)\n        raw, finish_reason = generate(title, content_to_send)\n        ai_title, ai_body  = parse_output(raw)\n        status = validate(ai_title, ai_body, finish_reason)\n        ratio  = bangla_ratio(ai_title + \" \" + ai_body)\n\n        df.at[i, \"ai_generated_news_title\"]   = ai_title\n        df.at[i, \"ai_generated_news_content\"] = ai_body\n        df.at[i, \"gen_status\"]        = status\n        df.at[i, \"finish_reason\"]     = finish_reason\n        df.at[i, \"source_truncated\"]  = bool(was_truncated)\n        df.at[i, \"bangla_ratio\"]      = round(ratio, 4)\n        df.at[i, \"body_words\"]        = len(ai_body.split())\n        df.at[i, \"gen_model\"]         = MODEL_NAME\n        df.at[i, \"gen_time_utc\"]      = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")\n\n        append_jsonl({\n            \"row\": int(i), \"part\": FILE_NUM, \"status\": status,\n            \"finish_reason\": finish_reason, \"source_truncated\": bool(was_truncated),\n            \"bangla_ratio\": round(ratio, 4), \"body_words\": len(ai_body.split()),\n            \"title\": ai_title, \"content\": ai_body,\n        })\n\n        if status != \"ok\":\n            print(f\"  row {i}: {status}\")\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        df.at[i, \"gen_status\"]   = f\"error: {type(e).__name__}\"\n        df.at[i, \"gen_time_utc\"] = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")\n        append_jsonl({\"row\": int(i), \"part\": FILE_NUM,\n                      \"status\": \"error\", \"message\": str(e)[:300]})\n        print(f\"  row {i} failed: {e}\")\n        if isinstance(e, RuntimeError):\n            print(\"All keys exhausted — stopping. Re-run tomorrow or add more keys.\")\n            break\n\n    processed += 1\n    if processed % SAVE_EVERY == 0:\n        atomic_to_excel(df, OUTPUT_PATH)\n\n    time.sleep(current_delay)\n\natomic_to_excel(df, OUTPUT_PATH)\nprint(f\"\\nSaved: {OUTPUT_PATH}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# CELL 5 — QUALITY REPORT\n# ============================================================\ndf = pd.read_excel(OUTPUT_PATH)\nok = df[df[\"gen_status\"] == \"ok\"]\n\nprint(f\"PART {FILE_NUM} — {len(df)} rows\\n\")\nprint(\"Status breakdown\")\nprint(df[\"gen_status\"].value_counts().to_string())\n\nif len(ok):\n    print(f\"\\nClean rows: {len(ok)} ({len(ok)/len(df):.1%})\")\n    print(f\"Body words   — mean {ok['body_words'].mean():.0f}, \"\n          f\"median {ok['body_words'].median():.0f}, \"\n          f\"p5 {ok['body_words'].quantile(.05):.0f}, \"\n          f\"p95 {ok['body_words'].quantile(.95):.0f}\")\n    print(f\"Bangla ratio — min {ok['bangla_ratio'].min():.3f}, \"\n          f\"mean {ok['bangla_ratio'].mean():.3f}\")\n    print(f\"Source truncated: {ok['source_truncated'].mean():.1%} of rows\")\n    print(f\"Output cut off  : {(df['finish_reason'] == 'length').mean():.1%} of rows\")\n\n    # export only clean rows for the training corpus\n    clean_path = os.path.join(WORKING_DIR, f\"ai_real_part_{FILE_NUM}_clean.xlsx\")\n    atomic_to_excel(\n        ok[[\"news_title\", \"news_content\",\n            \"ai_generated_news_title\", \"ai_generated_news_content\", \"body_words\"]],\n        clean_path)\n    print(f\"\\nClean export: {clean_path}\")\n\nbad = df[~df[\"gen_status\"].isin([\"ok\", \"\"])]\nif len(bad):\n    print(f\"\\n{len(bad)} rows need a re-run — set RETRY_FAILURES = True and re-run Cell 4.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-16T19:52:47.313475Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-16T19:52:47.314445Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-16T19:52:47.31417Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-16T19:52:47.314209Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n\n## Length-parity check (run once, after both classes exist)\n\nThis is the diagnostic your defense will hinge on. If AI-real and AI-fake differ\nsystematically in length, a classifier can score high without ever learning anything\nabout fabrication.\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score\n\nreal = pd.read_excel(\"ai_real_all.xlsx\")\nfake = pd.read_excel(\"ai_fake_all.xlsx\")\n\ndef feats(df):\n    t = df[\"ai_generated_news_content\"].astype(str)\n    return pd.DataFrame({\n        \"n_words\":     t.str.split().str.len(),\n        \"n_chars\":     t.str.len(),\n        \"n_sents\":     t.str.count(\"।\") + 1,\n        \"avg_wordlen\": t.str.len() / t.str.split().str.len().clip(lower=1),\n    })\n\nX = pd.concat([feats(real), feats(fake)]).fillna(0)\ny = [0] * len(real) + [1] * len(fake)\n\nscore = cross_val_score(LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000), X, y, cv=5).mean()\nprint(f\"Length-only baseline: {score:.1%}\")\n```\n\nRead it like this: **~50%** means length carries no signal and your 98.30% is real\ncontent learning — say so in the defense. **65-75%** means a meaningful share of your\naccuracy is a length artifact and you should length-match the two classes before\nretraining. Either way you want the number in hand before someone else asks for it.","metadata":{}}]}